    "body": "## Summary\n\nRestore plan reuse when packed THD sequence counts fall within the same batch bucket. Direct cumulative-length inputs contain only `actual_batch + 1` entries, so they cannot safely describe a larger bucketed batch without preparation.\n\nUse the existing length and offset conversions for bucketed ragged graphs. This supplies the bucket-sized metadata and lets those calls share forward plans. Dense/nonbucketed direct paths and backward behavior are unchanged.\n\nThe cache regression repacks a fixed token count into different sequence counts and checks forward/backward graph and plan reuse.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe restored source matches the earlier revision `4705bb6b`, which passed native output/gradient reference checks on GB200 with CUDA 13.5, cuDNN 9.25 and Frontend 1.29. Scoped pre-commit hooks and whitespace checks pass for the revert. Full frontend integration suites were not run locally; see [CI checks](https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/3700/checks).\n",
